        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            Peeling epoxy is a symptom, not a diagnosis. Sheets with clean concrete underneath mean prep or contamination; tire-shaped patches mean hot tire pickup; edges and joints mean moisture; one coat lifting off another means a missed recoat window. Read the floor before you buy anything.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Fix the cause, not the flake. Grind rather than etch, test for moisture before you coat, use a 100 per cent solids system with a real topcoat, and keep the car off it for a week. Do those four things and you will not read this page again.
          </p>
        </div>

